layName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Artemi Panarin scores twice and the Kings beat the Islanders in OT for a 2nd straight win","description":"— Artemi Panarin had two goals, Brandt Clarke scored in overtime and the Los Angeles Kings won a second consecutive game, 3-2 at the New York Islanders on Thursday night.","story":"NEW YORK -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3891952/artemi-panarin\">Artemi Panarin</a> had two goals, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874722/brandt-clarke\">Brandt Clarke</a> scored in overtime and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a> won a second consecutive game, 3-2 at the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              The Kings have back-to-back victories after losing their first six games. They were <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/kings-first-win-season-capitals-d29f5598b5f712b3d532c21fa4aa8095\">the final NHL team without</a> a win before <a href=\"https://apnews.com/9767bca46c327d2c4a99af4ca0493159\">defeating Washington</a> on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              LA was outplayed for much of the Islanders game and outshot 43-26. Panarin beat rusty backup <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3759/semyon-varlamov\">Semyon Varlamov</a> glove side twice, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2610321/darcy-kuemper\">Darcy Kuemper</a> kept making stops even as his rebound control was lacking, finishing with 41 saves.\n\n\r\n              Kuemper cracked for the first time with just under six minutes left in the second period when rookie Victor Eklund’s shot squeezed through on a power play. Islanders face of the franchise <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291933/matthew-schaefer\">Matthew Schaefer</a> wired a wrist shot by Kuemper 7:06 into the third.\n\n\r\n              Clarke scored the winner with 2:18 left in 3-on-3 OT after he and his teammates possessed the puck for several shifts in a row.\n\n\r\n              Varlamov, the 38-year-old making his first home start since Nov. 25, 2024, following double partial knee replacements, denied <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114802/adrian-kempe\">Adrian Kempe</a> on a penalty shot and made some big-time saves after giving up the soft goals to Panarin on the Kings' first five shots.\n\n\r\n              Panarin has four points in two games after four combined over the first six.\n\n\r\n              LA forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697383/quinton-byfield\">Quinton Byfield</a> was out after getting hurt against the Capitals. Byfield did not take part in the morning skate and is considered day to day with an upper-body injury.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Kings: Visit the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> on Saturday in the third of five games on their road trip.\n\n\r\n              Islanders: Open a three-game Western Conference trip Sunday at the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/dal/dallas-stars\">Dallas Stars</a>.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-23T02:29:08Z"}}